analysis:
The supplied units are documentation-only changes to docs/provider/cli-reference.md. Unit :4 and :5 are base text from line 1021 onward and unit :6 is head text from line 1. No executable source, authorization logic, attestation verification or coordinator code is changed in what I was given, so there are no concrete security regressions.

The changed text documents:
- an interactive-terminal sudo prompt for MDM profile inventory during `darkbloom unenroll`;
- the `--keep-serving` macOS 27+ App Attest migration, which requires fresh coordinator removal approval;
- the macOS-below-27 upgrade notice;
- the App Attest diagnostics reported by `report`, `doctor` and `logs`;
- the model switch and drain behavior.

These statements agree with the TB-011, T-052..T-058 and TB-002 model. The docs say App Attest diagnostics are untrusted context, unqualified or unsupported choices never fall back to cleanup, and device-wide DeviceCheck observations are bounded and not attributable. The docs also state that the report uses a closed pattern and drops message text, key identifiers and paths. That matches the T-058 privacy posture.

Coverage limits: the head text I received ends partway through the enroll/unenroll section, and the diff hunks were not supplied, so I could not isolate exactly which lines changed. The implementation behind these documented claims (Swift unenroll, report, App Attest code) was not supplied, so I cannot confirm that the docs match the code. A later pass would need that source to verify the documentation-versus-code claims. I do not consider this to affect a security conclusion for this PR.
